 ## Overview
-This method reconstructs a triangle mesh from a Signed Distance Function (SDF) by evaluating the function on a regular grid of cubes, filtering out cubes that are too far from the surface (narrow-band filtering), and applying the standard Marching Cubes algorithm to the remaining intersected cubes [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard Marching Cubes by skipping the vast majority of the domain volume, significantly reducing computation time for sparse or bounded surfaces [S1, unofficial].
+This method reconstructs a triangle mesh from a Signed Distance Function (SDF) by evaluating the field on a structured grid, filtering out cubes that are too far from the isosurface (narrow-band filtering), and applying the standard Marching Cubes algorithm to the remaining cubes [S1, unofficial]. It differs from naive Marching Cubes by skipping the vast majority of voxels that do not intersect the surface, significantly reducing computation time for sparse or bounded domains [S1, unofficial].
 
